2026-05-26 14:25:18,098 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: To address the tender's demands for strict GDPR compliance and explicability of AI recommendations, we can leverage our existing certifications and capabilities. Our ISO 27001 certification, which covers the design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems, demonstrates our commitment to security and data protection. Additionally, having a GDPR Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed and reachable at dpo@nexus-engineering.it ensures we have the necessary expertise in-house to navigate GDPR requirements.

For EU-only hosting and no data transfer outside the EU, our standard data residency policy already specifies that data should reside within the EU, aligning with this requirement. To further reinforce this, we can utilize our experience with SecNumCloud projects, ensuring that any infrastructure used for hosting meets the high security standards expected.

Encryption of sensitive data is a critical component of GDPR compliance. While our context does not explicitly mention encryption methods, our ISO 27001 certification and experience with risk management (ISO 27005) imply that we have the capability to implement appropriate encryption measures to protect sensitive data.

Regarding explicability of AI recommendations and ensuring all decisions are validated by an agent without automation, our AI security controls include output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation. These controls can help ensure that AI-driven recommendations are transparent and reliable. Moreover, our model isolation approach, where end-users do not have direct access to models but interact through an inference API, can facilitate the validation process by agents.

Our audit capabilities, including all queries being logged with immutability ensured through append-only logs with SHA-256 hash chaining, and real-time SIEM integration, will help in maintaining a compliant and secure environment. This is crucial for monitoring and demonstrating GDPR compliance, especially considering our ability to conduct Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs) with an average duration of 3 weeks.

Given our experience with EU regulatory frameworks such as the GDPR, NIS2 Directive, and eIDAS, we are well-positioned to ensure that all regulatory requirements are met. Our capability to provide anonymization tools, such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models, can further support GDPR compliance by ensuring that personal data is appropriately protected.

In summary, by leveraging our current certifications, GDPR instruments, AI security controls, audit capabilities, and experience with EU regulatory frameworks, we can implement the necessary security controls and regulatory compliance measures to meet the tender's demands for strict GDPR compliance and explicability of AI recommendations.
